  m_text: "High School Prerequisites To be admitted from an Ontario high school into
    the UWindsor BComm program, you must have completed ENG4U (Grade 12 English)
    and at least one Grade 12 U-level Mathematics course\u200B UWINDSOR.CA . A minimum
    70% grade in a 4U math is normally required, and the overall admission average
    (Top 6 Grade 12 U/M courses) should be at least 73% (approximately mid-70s)\u200B
    UWINDSOR.CA . The co-op stream is more competitive, typically requiring around
    a 78% average or higher for direct entry\u200B UWINDSOR.CA . It\u2019s recommended
    to take courses like Advanced Functions, Calculus and Vectors, or Data Management
    in high school to prepare for the quantitative aspects of the program. Strong
    English and communication skills are also important, as evidenced by the required
    ENG4U credit. (Learn more: Visit UWindsor\u2019s Admission Requirements for Business
    Administration.)"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
